Oxikube GPUI overlay patch: fetch the next drawable off the main thread
Crate: gpui-pre-apple 0.3.7 (crates.io, Apache-2.0; snapshot of zed-industries/zed@1a28cff,
Copyright Zed Industries, Inc. and contributors). Zed path: crates/gpui_apple/src/
Upstream: Zed PR draft "gpui_apple: Prefetch the next CAMetalLayer drawable on a worker thread"
(not yet filed; Oxikube issue karan-vk/Oxikube#601). Drop this patch at the first gpui-pre bump
that contains the fix.
Patch: Copyright Oxikube contributors, GPL-3.0-or-later (see patches/gpui/README.md).

Why: `MetalRenderer::draw` called `-[CAMetalLayer nextDrawable]` on the main thread, after
the frame's layout and paint. When the window draws every refresh all drawables are in use, so
it blocked until the window server released one; when that came late (or a resize had to
allocate new drawables) the main thread missed the next display-link callback (E05-P601: 5 to 10
ms waits, refreshes dropped). A worker thread now asks for the next drawable as soon as a frame
is handed to Core Animation, so the wait overlaps the next frame's layout and paint. At most one
drawable is held, so the layer's drawable count is unchanged; one of a stale size is returned
to the layer when the window resizes.
